# Hono Zod validation

Validate HTTP bodies and query strings with `@hono/zod-validator` wrappers in `apps/api/src/http/validate.ts`.

- Schemas live in `apps/api/src/http/schemas.ts`.
- Attach `zJson(schema)` or `zQuery(schema)` on the route.
- Handlers read `c.req.valid("json")` or `c.req.valid("query")`.
- Map Zod failures to RealWorld `FieldErrors` via `AppError("validation", …)`.

```ts
// BAD — hand-rolled parse helpers beside the router
const input = parseRegister(await c.req.json());

// GOOD
api.post("/users", zJson(registerJson), async (c) => {
  const input = c.req.valid("json");
  // ...
});
```

Do not resurrect `parse.ts` or a parallel parse-helper layer.

Prefer typed exceptions (`HTTPException` for malformed JSON) over string-sniffing error messages.

Keep `AppError` → HTTP status mapping literal and explicit.
